    "description": "Key Responsibilities Requirements Analysis & Test Planning Review business requirements, user stories, technical specifications, and acceptance criteria to identify gaps, ambiguities, testability issues, and quality risks early in the development cycle. Define risk-based test strategies and test plans covering scope, approach, test levels, test types, environments, test data, entry/exit criteria, and schedules. Design, document, and maintain test scenarios and test cases with clear traceability to requirements and acceptance criteria. Functional, Integration & Regression Testing Execute manual and exploratory testing to validate functionality, usability, and reliability against defined requirements. Perform integration testing to validate interactions between application modules, backend services, APIs, payment gateways, and other third-party systems. Plan and maintain regression test suites to ensure new features, enhancements, and defect fixes do not adversely affect existing functionality. Conduct smoke, sanity, and post-deployment verification testing across development, staging, and production environments. Perform cross-browser, cross-device, and responsive testing to ensure consistent behavior across all supported platforms. Test Automation Design, develop, and maintain scalable and maintainable automated UI, API, and end-to-end (E2E) test suites using frameworks such as Playwright, Cypress, or Selenium WebDriver, with test runners such as TestNG, JUnit, or equivalent. Identify and prioritize test cases suitable for automation based on business criticality, execution frequency, and return on investment, in line with the test automation pyramid. API Testing Perform comprehensive API testing using tools such as Postman and Newman, or code-based frameworks, to validate endpoints, HTTP methods and status codes, request/response payloads, schema contracts, error handling, authentication, and authorization. Validate third-party and internal service integrations, including negative, boundary, and failure-path scenarios. Database Testing Conduct database testing using SQL and NoSQL queries to verify data integrity, consistency, referential relationships, constraints, and transaction accuracy (ACID compliance where applicable). Validate data migrations, data transformations, and backend data flows triggered by application operations. Performance Testing Design and execute load, stress, spike, endurance, and concurrency tests using tools such as Apache JMeter, k6, or equivalent. Analyze key performance metrics (response time, throughput, error rate, and resource utilization) to identify bottlenecks and validate performance against defined service-level objectives. Security Testing Perform application and API security testing focused on authentication, authorization, session management, access control, and input validation. Test for common vulnerabilities based on the OWASP Top 10 and OWASP API Security Top 10, and support the security team with vulnerability assessments and remediation verification. CI/CD Integration & Release Readiness Collaborate with development and DevOps teams to integrate automated test suites into CI/CD pipelines (e.g., Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) to enable continuous testing and early defect detection. Define and maintain quality gates within pipelines and support release validation activities. Provide formal QA sign-off and evidence-based release readiness recommendations prior to production deployment. Defect Management Identify, document, and track defects using tools such as Jira or equivalent, including clear reproduction steps, expected versus actual results, environment details, and supporting evidence. Classify defects by severity and priority, participate in defect triage, and verify fixes through retesting and regression. Perform root cause analysis on critical and escaped defects to prevent recurrence. Quality Reporting & Metrics Prepare test summary reports and monitor key quality indicators, including requirements and test coverage, test execution results, defect density and trends, regression status, automation coverage, and production defect leakage. Communicate quality status, risks, and recommendations clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders. Collaboration, Documentation & Continuous Improvement Collaborate with developers, product managers, designers, and other stakeholders to clarify requirements and ensure acceptance criteria are met. Actively participate in Agile/Scrum ceremonies, including backlog refinement, sprint planning, daily stand-ups, sprint reviews, and retrospectives. Maintain up-to-date documentation of test plans, test cases, test data, test environments, and test results. Continuously evaluate and improve testing processes, tools, frameworks, and standards to increase test effectiveness and team efficiency.",
