    "description": "JOB PURPOSE/OBJECTIVES The Project Manager is responsible for overseeing and managing investment projects from inception to completion. This role involves planning, coordinating, budgeting, and supervising investment projects to ensure they are completed on time, within scope, and within budget. The Project Manager will work closely with architects, engineers, contractors and Promasidor engineering teams to deliver high-quality finishing. He is the number one responsible for construction workplace safety all through the project. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES/ACTIVITIES Project Planning and Scheduling Develop comprehensive project plans outlining the scope, goals, deliverables, resources, budget, accountabilities and timeline. Create and maintain project schedules, ensuring timely completion of all phases of the project. Budget Management Prepare and manage project budgets, track expenses, and ensure cost control. Conduct financial analysis and reporting, ensuring projects stay within budget. Resource Management Coordinate and allocate resources effectively, including project staff, materials, and equipment are accounted for during the duration of the project from start to finish Manage contractors, suppliers, and consultants, ensuring timely delivery of services and materials. 4. Quality Control and Compliance Ensure all construction activities comply with relevant building codes, safety regulations, and quality standards (high level of finishing). Conduct regular inspections and audits to ensure project quality and safety. 5. Stakeholder Communication Serve as the primary point of contact for Promasidor, contractors, suppliers, consultants, and other stakeholders. Facilitate regular meetings to update stakeholders on project progress and address any issues. 6. Risk Management Identify potential risks and develop mitigation strategies. Monitor and manage project risks and issues, ensuring timely resolution. 7. Project Governance, Documentation and Reporting Maintain comprehensive project documentation, including contracts, change orders, and progress reports. Prepare and present regular progress reports to senior management and stakeholders. 8. Team Leadership Lead and motivate project teams, fostering a collaborative and productive work environment. Provide mentorship and guidance to junior staff and project team members. 9. Safety Management Ensure safety culture implementation in all investment project activities, from conception to hand over to production team. Ensure all project stakeholders adhere to safety plans and implement required safety measures. Provide required support to the project safety officer to minimise safety incidents on construction site. 10. Project Completion and Closure Monitor closely every phase/milestone of the project and ensure sign off before contractors and paid off Ensure that the formal project completion certificate is signed off as per the agreed terms and conditions of the project KEY ACTIVITIES / PERFORMANCE AREAS & MEASURES PERFORMANCE AREAS Timeliness of Project delivery Budget Management Alignment with Company Goals",
